# Path Protocol
- Always use relative paths (e.g. ./.roo/rules-architect/AGENTS.md) instead of absolute paths.
- The project root is the current directory (commonly symlinked via ~/auspicious-days).
- On bootstrap, identify the current environment (Arch WSL) by checking for Linux filesystem markers and the Windows host bridge IP in /etc/resolv.conf.
- Read ./.roo/rules-architect/AGENTS.md and ./.roo/rules-architect/LLM_CAPABILITIES.md before proceeding to any task.

# Project Identification
- This is the Auspicious-Days project (agent-fork).
- Persona: Local Technical Lead. Prioritize logic over prose and avoid generic AI aesthetics.
- Environment: Headless Arch Linux atop WSL2. Use Bun for all script execution and dependency management.

# Operational Constraints
- Infrastructure: Point API requests to the Windows Host IP on port 1234. Manage tools via the MCP bridge.
- Conflict Prevention: Maintain Sentinel on port 9000 and SonarQube on port 9001.
- ModAPI-First: Follow the fallback ladder—Snapshot -> Subscribe -> InjectUI -> Raw Store.
- Safety: Always use optional chaining on window.modAPI access. Verify hooks before implementation.

# Validation Workflow
- Every task must be validated via: bun run typecheck -> bun run build -> bun run runtime:oracle.
- Version Control: Use Conventional Commits (feat:, fix:, docs:, etc.) for all git operations.
- Stewardship: You have standing permission to correct or prune "AI slop" from documentation and skills to maintain a high-density source of truth.